{"name":"Plumage","hex":"#00998c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"plumage","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The feathers covering the body of a bird collectively.","Feathers used ornamentally; feathering;  a bunch or tuft of such feathers; a plume.\n\n Feathers which are fed to a hawk to cause it to regurgitate, for the purpose of cleaning its crop; a type of casting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plumage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Plumage","blocks":[{"text":"Plumage, or feathering, is a layer of feathers that covers a bird and the pattern, colour, and arrangement of those feathers. The pattern and colours of plumage differ between species and subspecies and may vary with sex and age classes. Within a few species, there can be different colour morphs. The placement of feathers on a bird is not haphazard but rather emerges in organised, overlapping rows and groups, and these feather tracts are known by standard names."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Plumage_house_sparrow.jpg/330px-Plumage_house_sparrow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plumage","wikidata":"Q3303665"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Mandarinducksum.JPG/500px-Mandarinducksum.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Mandarinducksum.JPG/500px-Mandarinducksum.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mandarin duck (male) in eclipse plumage","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMandarinducksum.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Guiraca_caeruleaAAP086CB.jpg/500px-Guiraca_caeruleaAAP086CB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com